":{"input_tokens":218152,"output_tokens":3233,"requests":8}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"5ba282ed59306db7e4e96a892684943db96ae8591d431abc9ef390555fa8b274"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":205068,"output_tokens":4158,"requests":8}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"df9294431a6cfc28d3a3e2c3507a28b7daaeca0cdce682376fe39ef379cd4bfc"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":38321,"output_tokens":1428,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"cabc8ed81ae11b324df8dc4ac3162008a3a79d6977855b2cd1b87239b93ea195"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":40446,"output_tokens":1469,"requests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"f0aaadcf23f3d698123c790ed4b2e0c303c9ef083bb2834186505cc9650ed483"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":94835,"output_tokens":3713,"requests":7}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the live diff handles a fail-soft link-axis read (issue_link_types() -> None, distinct from checked-and-empty []): degrade that axis to its own could-not-check `unavailable` finding rather than diffing configured link values against a None/empty set (which would false-positive every configured link value as drift).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["mapping_probe.py:144-149 — issue_link_types() '``could-not-check must stay distinguishable from checked-and-empty: a failed read degrades to ``None``, never ``[]``'","The plan enumerates link among the diffed axes but its failure-case reasoning stops at whole-probe failure/timeout; a PARTIAL (single-axis) fail-soft read on the link axis is unaddressed","G6 checklist item 1: edge/empty/failure cases must be handled — an axis-level fail-soft None is an unhandled failure case"],"finding":"The live-drift mechanism does not handle the reused S8 probe reader's fail-soft link-axis read: mapping_probe.issue_link_types() returns None (could-not-check), distinct from [] (checked-and-empty). The plan diffs the link axis as 'a configured value absent from Jira's set' but never says what happens when the observed link set is None — diffing configured link values against None/empty would report every configured link value as drift (a false-positive storm), or silently drop the axis.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd9c70869215eff96","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach § Live-drift check: 'diff configured vs observed vocabulary, one finding per divergence on the axes the reader observes — status, type, link (a configured value absent from Jira's set)'","norm_id":"nc55abacd941a7a71","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Jira reachable and status/type read fine, but the link-types endpoint read fails soft (returns None) — without handling, every configured link value is reported as absent-from-Jira drift"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"In the live-drift section, add: when the probe reader returns None for an axis (could-not-check, e.g. link-types fail-soft), emit one distinct per-axis unavailable finding for that axis and skip diffing it, while still diffing the axes that were observed.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respec